        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "The `queued` timestamp is wrong for every assignment source. It is the worker's import time, not the enqueue time, and gets older the longer the process runs. Any logic that relies on it gets incorrect results.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "`queued: datetime = timezone.now()` is evaluated when the class body runs, at module import. Every AssignmentSource built through from_integration (sync.py lines 98 and 115) gets the same process-start timestamp as `queued`, not the time it was created. to_dict then sends that stale value to the Celery task. If anything uses `queued` to order or dedupe assignment events, it will see wrong values. The field needs `field(default_factory=timezone.now)`.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "start_line": 18
        },
        "other_findings": [],
        "prior_findings": [],
        "replacement": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "original": "    queued: datetime = timezone.now()",
          "start_line": 18,
          "text": "    queued: datetime = field(default_factory=timezone.now)"
        },
